  "worked_solution": "Remember that the square root of a perfect square can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nAlso, we notice that ${a}^{2}$ and ${b}^{2}$ are perfect squares.\n\nFirst, we write the expression under the square root as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}{b}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{a\\cdot a\\cdot b\\cdot b} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{a\\cdot b\\cdot a\\cdot b} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(ab)\\cdot (ab)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(ab)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the absolute value of the squared quantity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(ab)^{2}} & =|ab|\\end{aligned}\n$$",
